## 7. Style Writing Rules

### Use Object Styles (Recommended)

**✅ Object Styles (Recommended):**

```typescript
const styles = css({
  display: 'flex',
  flexDirection: 'column',
  padding: '16px',
  backgroundColor: '#ffffff',
  '&:hover': {
    backgroundColor: '#f5f5f5',
  },
  '@media (min-width: 768px)': {
    flexDirection: 'row',
  },
})
```

**vs. String Styles:**

```typescript
const styles = css`
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  padding: 16px;
  background-color: #ffffff;

  &:hover {
    background-color: #f5f5f5;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    flex-direction: row;
  }
`
```

### Object Styles Benefits:

- Better type checking
- IDE autocomplete support
- camelCase property names (JavaScript convention)
- Catch errors at compile time instead of runtime
- Better performance (no parsing needed)

